BUG2022042401814: Weedout gives an incorrect result because of PTRC
Following test case tries to simulate PTRC is disabled during execution
when hit ratio is too lower. Here we set check frequency to low value to
make hit ratio be checked with fewer records reading.
SET rds_partial_result_cache_cost_threshold = 0;
SET @old_threshold = @@rds_partial_result_cache_hit_ratio_frequency;
SET rds_partial_result_cache_hit_ratio_frequency = 4;
SELECT * FROM t2 WHERE t2.b IN (SELECT t1.a FROM t1, t2 AS t3 WHERE t1.b>t3.b);
a	b
1	3
1	3
1	3
1	3
SET rds_partial_result_cache_hit_ratio_frequency = @old_threshold;
SET optimizer_switch = @save_optimizer_switch;
DROP TABLE t1, t2;
BUG2022042401814: Weedout gives an incorrect result because of PTRC
Another weedout case which can check weedout can give a bad result if
PTRC doesn't cache rowid.
